{"total_count":31,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528","id":4925479210,"node_id":"I_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAABJZTZKg","number":34528,"title":"Source control push panel does not show deleted tags as a change","user":{"login":"Marshall-Qiu","id":89381510,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MzgxNTEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89381510?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu","html_url":"https://github.com/Marshall-Qiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9542225587,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLOsw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:in-linear","name":"status:in-linear","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Issue or PR is now in Linear"},{"id":9542227923,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLX0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:team-assigned","name":"status:team-assigned","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"A team has been assigned the issue or PR"},{"id":10081993897,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACWO8EqQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/team:lifecycle","name":"team:lifecycle","color":"7A36AC","default":false,"description":"Issue is with the Lifecycle & Governance team"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-07-20T03:17:55Z","updated_at":"2026-07-20T09:02:12Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Bug Description\n\nOn an instance connected to source control (Environments feature), deleting a tag is not surfaced as a pending change in the source control push panel. The deletion therefore never gets committed to the git repository, and instances that pull from the same repository keep the deleted tag indefinitely.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Set up two instances connected to the same source control repository (one push instance, one pull/protected instance), following the Environments docs.\n2. On the push instance, create a tag, assign it to a workflow, and push so `tags.json` in the repo contains it.\n3. On the push instance, delete the tag.\n4. Open the source control push panel (Commit and push).\n5. Observe: no pending change is listed for the deleted tag, so the deletion cannot be pushed. Pull instances continue to show the tag.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nDeleting a tag should appear as a `tags` change with status `deleted` in the push panel, and pushing should update `tags.json` in the repository so pull instances remove the tag as well.\n\n### Debug Info\n\nObserved on self-hosted 2.26.3 with the Environments/source control feature licensed and enabled, in a two-instance setup (build instance pushes, protected production instance pulls).\n\n### Operating System\n\nLinux (Kubernetes)\n\n### n8n Version\n\n2.26.3\n\n### Node.js Version\n\n22.x\n\n### Database\n\nPostgreSQL\n\n### Execution Mode\n\nqueue\n\n### Hosting\n\nself hosted","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/32886","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/32886/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/32886/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/32886/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/32886","id":4729050700,"node_id":"I_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAABGd-WTA","number":32886,"title":"Source Control: support GitHub App authentication (auto-refreshed installation tokens)","user":{"login":"DrFaust92","id":33663870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNjYzODcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33663870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrFaust92","html_url":"https://github.com/DrFaust92","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrFaust92/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrFaust92/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrFaust92/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrFaust92/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrFaust92/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrFaust92/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrFaust92/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrFaust92/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrFaust92/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8864809689,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACEGJC2Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/closed:enhancement/feature","name":"closed:enhancement/feature","color":"191de0","default":false,"description":"Issue was closed as it was an enhancement or feature request."}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-06-23T19:46:32Z","updated_at":"2026-06-23T19:46:49Z","closed_at":"2026-06-23T19:46:49Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Is your feature request related to a problem?\n\nn8n Source Control (Environments) currently authenticates to the Git remote with either an **SSH deploy key** or **HTTPS username/password**. For HTTPS, the password is a static token (PAT). Static tokens have two problems for org-managed deployments:\n\n1. **They expire.** When a static HTTPS token expires, source control breaks — and per #28311 an expired token can even **prevent n8n from starting after a restart**. Someone has to manually rotate the secret.\n2. **They're coarse / long-lived.** PATs are tied to a user account and are broadly scoped; SSH deploy keys are per-repo but are long-lived static secrets with no built-in rotation.\n\nFor organizations syncing workflows to GitHub, a **GitHub App** is the standard, recommended auth model: org-installable, fine-grained repo permissions, and **short-lived installation access tokens (~1h) that are minted on demand** rather than stored long-term.\n\n## Describe the solution you'd like\n\nAdd a third source-control connection type for **GitHub App** authentication. n8n would store the App credentials (App ID, Installation ID, App private key) encrypted in the existing source-control settings, and **mint a fresh installation access token at git-client initialization**, feeding it into the Git remote over HTTPS.\n\nThis fits the existing architecture with minimal new plumbing:\n\n- The HTTPS path already injects credentials via a git `credential.helper` (`username` / `password`). A GitHub App installation token slots straight in as `username=x-access-token`, `password=<installation-token>`.\n- The git client is already rebuilt per operation, so minting the token at init avoids any long-lived refresh daemon — and the ~1h TTL is never a problem because every operation gets a fresh token.\n- Encrypted secret storage already exists (SSH key + HTTPS creds use the same `Cipher` + Settings pattern); the App private key would reuse it.\n\nSketch of the changes: extend the `connectionType` enum (`'ssh' | 'https'` → add `'github_app'`), add App fields to the preferences DTO/service, and in the git service mint the installation token (JWT signed with the App key → `POST /app/installations/{id}/access_tokens`) before building the existing HTTPS credential helper. Plus a settings-UI form for the App credentials.\n\n## Describe alternatives you've considered\n\n- **Static HTTPS PAT** (works today) — but expires and breaks sync/startup (#28311), and needs manual rotation.\n- **SSH deploy key** (works today) — long-lived static secret, no rotation, per-repo management overhead at org scale.\n- A GitHub App's auto-refreshed installation tokens avoid both: no stored long-lived credential to leak, automatic expiry/rotation, and fine-grained org-level control.\n\n## Additional context\n\nDirectly addresses the failure mode in #28311 (expired HTTPS token blocks startup) — installation tokens are minted fresh per operation, so there's no static token to expire.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/32886/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/32886/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/30888","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/30888/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/30888/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/30888/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/30888","id":4494119732,"node_id":"I_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAABC97TNA","number":30888,"title":"Enterprise GIT & Project Deletion Fails with Large Set of Executions","user":{"login":"erictmnz","id":179191187,"node_id":"U_kgDOCq49kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/179191187?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erictmnz","html_url":"https://github.com/erictmnz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erictmnz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erictmnz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erictmnz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erictmnz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erictmnz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erictmnz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erictmnz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erictmnz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erictmnz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9542225587,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLOsw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:in-linear","name":"status:in-linear","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Issue or PR is now in Linear"},{"id":9542227923,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLX0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:team-assigned","name":"status:team-assigned","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"A team has been assigned the issue or PR"},{"id":10081993897,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACWO8EqQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/team:lifecycle","name":"team:lifecycle","color":"7A36AC","default":false,"description":"Issue is with the Lifecycle & Governance team"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-05-21T11:24:32Z","updated_at":"2026-07-21T08:10:10Z","closed_at":"2026-07-16T19:35:32Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Bug Description\n\nWhen using the Source Control (Git) enterprise feature to pull the latest version in an environment, if the incoming changeset includes the deletion of a project, the pull operation fails silently and never completes. \nThe root cause is that n8n's internal deleteProject call times out with a QueryFailedError: canceling statement due to statement timeout when attempting to bulk-delete workflow executions belonging to the project, causing the entire Git pull to be aborted without surfacing a clear user-facing error. The operation succeeded when run manually after ~9 minutes, but by that point the Git pull had already been abandoned by n8n.\n\nThe Git pull only succeeds after manually deleting the project (and its associated workflows and executions) directly from the database.\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n1. Create a team project in n8n with a large number of workflows and/or workflow executions.\n2. In a connected Git branch, delete the project (remove all associated workflow files and project config).\n3. Commit and push those changes to the remote branch.\n4. In the n8n production instance, navigate to **Settings → Source Control** and trigger a **Pull** from the remote.\n5. Observe that the pull operation fails/hangs. The instance logs will show:\n   ```\n   QueryFailedError: canceling statement due to statement timeout\n       at PostgresQueryRunner.query (...)\n       at DeleteQueryBuilder.execute (...)\n       at WorkflowService.delete (workflow.service.ts:916)\n       at ProjectService.deleteProject (project.service.ee.ts:159)\n       at ProjectController.deleteProject (project.controller.ts:370)\n   ```\n6. The Git pull never succeeds until the project, workflows, and executions are manually removed from the database.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe Source Control pull should either:\n\nSuccessfully apply the project deletion (including all workflows and their executions) without timing out, even when the execution history is large; or\nHandle the timeout gracefully, retry the deletion asynchronously, and still allow the Git pull to complete (or roll back cleanly with a meaningful error surfaced in the UI).\nThe Git pull should never be left in a broken/incomplete state due to a downstream DB timeout during project deletion.\n\n### Debug Info\n\nQueryFailedError: canceling statement due to statement timeout\n    at PostgresQueryRunner.query (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/n8n/node_modules/.pnpm/@n8n+typeorm@0.3.20-17_.../src/driver/postgres/PostgresQueryRunner.ts:331:19)\n    at processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:104:5)\n    at DeleteQueryBuilder.execute (...DeleteQueryBuilder.ts:77:33)\n    at WorkflowService.delete (...workflow.service.ts:916:3)\n    at ProjectService.deleteProject (...project.service.ee.ts:159:5)\n    at ProjectController.deleteProject (...project.controller.ts:370:3)\n    at handler (...controller.registry.ts:111:12)\n    at .../response-helper.ts:118:17\n\nTimestamp: 2026-05-21T10:27:34Z\nQuery duration before timeout: ~9 minutes (query eventually completed successfully when run manually)\n\n### Operating System\n\nAzure Container Apps\n\n### n8n Version\n\n2.22.0\n\n### Node.js Version\n\n24.15.0\n\n### Database\n\nPostgreSQL\n\n### Execution mode\n\nqueue\n\n### Hosting\n\nself hosted","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/30888/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/30888/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/27160","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/27160/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/27160/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/27160/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/27160","id":4088620748,"node_id":"I_kwDOC4Q8Qs7zs2bM","number":27160,"title":"Git integration resets non-default credential option values (custom credentials)","user":{"login":"lennartki","id":47004085,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDA0MDg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47004085?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lennartki","html_url":"https://github.com/lennartki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lennartki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lennartki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lennartki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lennartki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lennartki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lennartki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lennartki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lennartki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lennartki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9542225587,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLOsw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:in-linear","name":"status:in-linear","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Issue or PR is now in Linear"},{"id":9542227923,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLX0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:team-assigned","name":"status:team-assigned","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"A team has been assigned the issue or PR"},{"id":10081993897,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACWO8EqQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/team:lifecycle","name":"team:lifecycle","color":"7A36AC","default":false,"description":"Issue is with the Lifecycle & Governance team"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-03-17T13:36:20Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T06:37:27Z","closed_at":"2026-08-17T13:23:41Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Bug Description\n\nWhen using Git-based source control in n8n, credential stubs are exported inconsistently depending on whether a property uses its default value or not. This causes issues with custom credentials that include option-type properties (e.g. environment selection).\n\nSpecifically:\n\n- If a credential property is set to its default value, it is omitted from the exported JSON.\n- If set to a non-default value, it is exported but with an empty string instead of the actual value.\n\nThis leads to environments being reset unintentionally when pulling from Git.\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n1. Create a custom credential with an options field (example below).\n2. Set the environment to the default value (Sandbox).\n3. Export via Git → observe that the environment field is omitted.\n4. Change environment to Production (non-default).\n5. Export via Git → observe that environment is included but empty (\"\").\n6. Pull credentials into another instance (e.g. production).\n\n**Example credential definition**\n```\nproperties: INodeProperties[] = [\n\t{\n\t\tdisplayName: 'APIKeyHeader',\n\t\tname: 'apikey',\n\t\ttype: 'string',\n\t\tdefault: '',\n\t\ttypeOptions: {\n\t\t\tpassword: true,\n\t\t}\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\tdisplayName: 'Environment',\n\t\tname: 'environment',\n\t\ttype: 'options',\n\t\toptions: [\n\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\tname: 'Production',\n\t\t\t\tvalue: 'https://api.postnl.nl',\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\tname: 'Sandbox',\n\t\t\t\tvalue: 'https://api-sandbox.postnl.nl',\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t],\n\t\tdefault: 'https://api-sandbox.postnl.nl',\n\t\trequired: true,\n\t}\n];\n```\n\n**Actual behavior**\n\nExported credential JSON:\n\n**Default value (Sandbox):**\n\n```\n\"data\": {\n  \"apikey\": \"\"\n}\n```\n\n\n**Non-default value (Production):**\n\n```\n\"data\": {\n  \"apikey\": \"\",\n  \"environment\": \"\"\n}\n```\n### Impact\nThis breaks multi-environment setups:\n\n- Test instance uses default (Sandbox)\n- Production uses non-default (Production)\n\nEach Git pull into production resets the environment back to default, causing incorrect API endpoints to be used.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n- The `environment` field should always be exported when required.\n- Pulling from Git should not reset credential values to defaults.\n\n### Debug Info\n\n# Debug info\n\n## core\n\n- n8nVersion: 2.13.0\n- platform: docker (self-hosted)\n- nodeJsVersion: 24.13.1\n- nodeEnv: production\n- database: postgres\n- executionMode: regular\n- concurrency: -1\n- license: enterprise (production)\n- consumerId: dd48394b-8e90-40b9-9c05-179ae02904ec\n\n## storage\n\n- success: all\n- error: all\n- progress: false\n- manual: true\n- binaryMode: filesystem\n\n## pruning\n\n- enabled: true\n- maxAge: 336 hours\n- maxCount: 10000 executions\n\n## client\n\n- userAgent: mozilla/5.0 (windows nt 10.0; win64; x64) applewebkit/537.36 (khtml, like gecko) chrome/142.0.0.0 safari/537.36 edg/142.0.0.0\n- isTouchDevice: false\n\nGenerated at: 2026-03-17T13:35:04.950Z\n\n### Operating System\n\nDocker\n\n### n8n Version\n\n2.13.0\n\n### Node.js Version\n\n24.13.1\n\n### Database\n\nPostgreSQL\n\n### Execution mode\n\nmain (default)\n\n### Hosting\n\nself hosted","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/27160/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/27160/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/29560","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/29560/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/29560/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/29560/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/29560","id":4356479017,"node_id":"I_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAABA6qYKQ","number":29560,"title":"Bug: Source control (git sync) overwrites credential port numbers, blocking per-environment values","user":{"login":"fank","id":1900106,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MDAxMDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1900106?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank","html_url":"https://github.com/fank","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9542225587,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLOsw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:in-linear","name":"status:in-linear","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Issue or PR is now in Linear"},{"id":9542227923,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLX0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:team-assigned","name":"status:team-assigned","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"A team has been assigned the issue or PR"},{"id":10081993897,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACWO8EqQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/team:lifecycle","name":"team:lifecycle","color":"7A36AC","default":false,"description":"Issue is with the Lifecycle & Governance team"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-04-30T08:17:54Z","updated_at":"2026-05-07T11:47:25Z","closed_at":"2026-05-07T11:47:25Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bug Description\n\nWhen using **Source Control (git sync)** to sync credentials between environments, numeric and boolean credential fields (notably **port**, but also flags like `allowUnauthorizedCerts` and numbers like `requestTimeout`) are pushed and pulled as part of the credential stub. This makes it impossible to maintain different ports for the same credential type in different environments, and any subsequent push from the source instance silently overwrites the local value on the pulling instance.\n\nConcrete example: Microsoft SQL credentials.\n\n- Instance A creates a Microsoft SQL credential with port `1533`.\n- A pushes — stub committed with `\"port\": 1533`.\n- Instance B pulls — gets a credential with empty strings (server/user/password) but `\"port\": 1533` already filled in from A.\n- Operator on B does initial setup on B: fills in server/user/password and sets B's own port `1433`.\n- Some time later A pushes again (e.g. unrelated edit, or because port shows as \"modified\" in the dialog with credentials checked by default).\n- B pulls — **B's port is silently overwritten back to 1533**, because numbers are not sanitized during sync.\n\nThe same applies to any credential where a numeric or boolean field legitimately differs per environment (any DB port, custom HTTP port, timeouts, TLS toggles, etc.).\n\nLikely related: #13966 — same root cause causes the credential not to be flagged as \"initial setup required\" on the pulling instance, because the synced stub already has non-empty `port`/`allowUnauthorizedCerts` values, so it doesn't look empty.\n\n## To Reproduce\n\n1. Connect two n8n instances (A and B) to the same source control repository.\n2. On A, create a Microsoft SQL credential with port `1533` and full server/user/password.\n3. Push from A.\n4. On B, pull. The credential appears with empty server/user/password but `port: 1533` already set.\n5. On B, do the initial setup: fill server/user/password and change port to `1433`.\n6. On A, edit the credential (or just trigger a push — the credential will appear as a modified candidate, checked by default).\n7. Push from A.\n8. On B, pull → B's port is silently changed back to `1533`. B's connection breaks.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nNumeric and boolean connection fields that legitimately differ per environment should not be force-synced. At minimum:\n\n- Numbers (and booleans) should be sanitized the same way string values are: only the schema/key is exported, the value is preserved per environment on pull.\n- Or, credential field metadata should let node authors mark fields as \"environment-local\" so they are excluded from the synced stub (e.g. an opt-in `noSync: true` on `INodeProperties`).\n\nEither way, after a sync the local value of `port` (and similar fields) on the pulling instance must not be silently overwritten. As a side effect this would also fix #13966, since with port/flags excluded the freshly-pulled stub would look empty and could properly trigger \\\"initial setup required\\\".\n\n## Root cause\n\n`sanitizeCredentialData` in `packages/cli/src/modules/source-control.ee/source-control-helper.ee.ts` deliberately strips strings to `''` but preserves numbers and booleans verbatim:\n\n```ts\n// packages/cli/src/modules/source-control.ee/source-control-helper.ee.ts\nexport function sanitizeCredentialData(\n  data: ICredentialDataDecryptedObject,\n): ICredentialDataDecryptedObject {\n  const result: ICredentialDataDecryptedObject = deepCopy(data);\n\n  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(data)) {\n    if (value === null || key === 'oauthTokenData') {\n      delete result[key];\n    } else if (typeof value === 'object') {\n      result[key] = sanitizeCredentialData(value as ICredentialDataDecryptedObject);\n    } else if (typeof value === 'string') {\n      result[key] = containsExpression(value) ? value : '';\n    }\n\n    // NOTE: number and boolean values are synchable for backward compatibility\n    // Typically numbers represent PORT numbers or other numeric values that aren't sensitives\n    // Boolean are usually represent non sensitive flags\n    // This could be revisited in the future\n  }\n\n  return result;\n}\n```\n\nThe accompanying comment explicitly anticipates this: numbers (\\\"typically PORT numbers\\\") are intentionally pushed through, which is exactly what makes per-environment ports impossible. Introduced/last touched in #25530 (\\\"fix: Enable credentials expressions push and pull\\\").\n\nConfirmed in a real sync repo: a Microsoft SQL stub serializes as\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"microsoftSql\",\n  \"data\": { \"server\": \"\", \"user\": \"\", \"password\": \"\", \"port\": 1533, \"requestTimeout\": 15000000 }\n}\n```\n— strings blanked, numbers preserved.\n\nThe Microsoft SQL credential definition (`packages/nodes-base/credentials/MicrosoftSql.credentials.ts`) declares `port` as `type: 'number'`, which is why this hits SQL credentials in particular, but the issue is general — any numeric or boolean field on any credential will behave the same way.\n\n## Suggested fix directions\n\n- Treat numbers and booleans the same as strings during sanitization (export schema only, preserve local value on pull). Simplest fix and matches the existing string behavior. Also fixes #13966 as a side effect.\n- Or, add an opt-in flag on `INodeProperties` (e.g. `noSync: true` / `environmentLocal: true`) so credential authors can mark fields that must not cross environments. `port`, `connectTimeout`, `requestTimeout`, `tls`, `allowUnauthorizedCerts` etc. on `MicrosoftSql` would then be marked accordingly.\n\nThe current backward-compatibility argument should be revisited — the comment in the code itself says \\\"This could be revisited in the future,\\\" and the practical cost of the current behavior is that multi-environment setups with differing ports are unusable through git sync.\n\n## Debug Info\n\n- n8n version: 2.18.4 (also reproducible on earlier versions; behavior present since #25530)\n- Source control: Enterprise git sync feature\n- Affected file: \\`packages/cli/src/modules/source-control.ee/source-control-helper.ee.ts\\` (\\`sanitizeCredentialData\\`)\n- Affected credential (example): \\`packages/nodes-base/credentials/MicrosoftSql.credentials.ts\\`\n- Related: #13966\n\n## Environment\n\n- Operating System: Linux (self-hosted on GKE)\n- n8n Version: 2.18.4\n- Node.js Version: 24.x\n- Database: PostgreSQL\n- Execution mode: queue\n- Hosting: self hosted","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/29560/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/29560/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21418","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21418/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21418/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21418/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21418","id":3574272217,"node_id":"I_kwDOC4Q8Qs7VCxDZ","number":21418,"title":"Environments: Git configuration via simple-git doesn`t respect the http/https proxy settings","user":{"login":"pharindoko","id":5619511,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTk1MTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5619511?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pharindoko","html_url":"https://github.com/pharindoko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pharindoko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pharindoko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pharindoko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pharindoko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pharindoko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pharindoko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pharindoko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pharindoko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pharindoko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8582015045,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAAB_4coRQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/team:payday","name":"team:payday","color":"ffffff","default":false,"description":"DEPRECATED LABEL"},{"id":9369676964,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACLnnspA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/triage:needs-info","name":"triage:needs-info","color":"FBCA04","default":false,"description":""},{"id":9542225587,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLOsw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:in-linear","name":"status:in-linear","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Issue or PR is now in Linear"},{"id":9542227923,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLX0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:team-assigned","name":"status:team-assigned","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"A team has been assigned the issue or PR"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2025-10-31T10:10:12Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T09:44:47Z","closed_at":"2026-07-14T09:44:47Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Bug Description\n\nI would like to setup the git-configuration with connection-type \"https\"\n\n<img width=\"1830\" height=\"469\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/35b305a5-1e9a-4238-9945-a98b6aee0fef\" /> \n\nbut I get a timeout when trying to connect due to our internal proxy blocking the request.\n\nI figured out that you use `simple-git` for it and it spawns up a child process and the Env variables setup for n8n are not passed to simpleGit.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n1. Go to \"Settings -> Environments\"\n2. Select \"Connection Type\" => \"HTTPS\"\n3. Set \"Username\" and \"Personal Access Token\"\n4. Click on \"Connect\"\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe environment variables for HTTP_PROXY/HTTPS_PROXY will be passed as Env to SimpleGit\n\nhttps://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/blob/c46d121bb4ce21ad083979f3d0d2f105287c601e/packages/nodes-base/nodes/Git/Git.node.ts#L310\n\n### Debug Info\n\nWe run into a timeout\n\n\n\n### Operating System\n\nn8n container\n\n### n8n Version\n\n1.117.2\n\n### Node.js Version\n\nn8n container\n\n### Database\n\nPostgreSQL\n\n### Execution mode\n\nmain (default)\n\n### Hosting\n\nself hosted","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21418/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21418/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21411","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21411/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21411/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21411/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21411","id":3573793871,"node_id":"I_kwDOC4Q8Qs7VA8RP","number":21411,"title":"Source Control: Unsynced Workflows Lost from Push Dialog After Admin Fails to Export Private Credentials","user":{"login":"bikalbasnet","id":7262965,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNjI5NjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7262965?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikalbasnet","html_url":"https://github.com/bikalbasnet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikalbasnet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikalbasnet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikalbasnet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikalbasnet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikalbasnet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikalbasnet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikalbasnet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikalbasnet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikalbasnet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8582015045,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAAB_4coRQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/team:payday","name":"team:payday","color":"ffffff","default":false,"description":"DEPRECATED LABEL"},{"id":9542225587,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLOsw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:in-linear","name":"status:in-linear","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Issue or PR is now in Linear"},{"id":9542227923,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLX0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:team-assigned","name":"status:team-assigned","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"A team has been assigned the issue or PR"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-10-31T08:05:21Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T09:44:51Z","closed_at":"2026-07-14T09:44:51Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Describe the problem/error/question\nThe **n8n Source Control** feature is **not properly detecting unsynced workflows/credentials** in the \"Push\" dialog after a **failed push attempt**.\n\nWhen a push attempt fails (e.g., due to an Instance Admin trying to push a personal/private credential which they do not have export permission for), the items that were part of the failed push are incorrectly removed from the list of unsynced changes in the \"Push\" dialog.\n\nThis issue is not limited to large pushes; it occurs even if only **one workflow or one credential** is part of the failed push.\n\nThis results in the Instance Admin being unable to see or attempt to push the unsynced workflows/credentials that failed previously. The dialog only shows newly created or modified items after the failure. The UI incorrectly assumes the failed items were actually pushed successfully, thus removing them from the unsynced list.\n\n## What is the error message (if any)?\nThe replicated failure (Instance Admin pushing a private credential / personal workflow) produced the error:\n**`Failed to export credentials to work folder`**\n\n## Please share your workflow/screenshots/recording\nN/A\n\n\n## Share the output returned by the last node\n(Not applicable as the issue occurs during the n8n Source Control push operation.)\n\n\n## Debug info\n\n### core\n\n- n8nVersion: 1.112.2\n- platform: docker (self-hosted)\n- nodeJsVersion: 22.18.0\n- nodeEnv: production\n- database: postgres\n- executionMode: regular\n- concurrency: -1\n- license: enterprise (production)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21411/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/21411/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/24692","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/24692/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/24692/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/24692/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/24692","id":3842517682,"node_id":"I_kwDOC4Q8Qs7lCCqy","number":24692,"title":"Published workflows which gets archived via source control are still active","user":{"login":"fank","id":1900106,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MDAxMDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1900106?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank","html_url":"https://github.com/fank","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":5176033697,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAABNIQBoQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/Needs%20Feedback","name":"Needs Feedback","color":"34F826","default":false,"description":"Waiting for further input or clarification."},{"id":9369676964,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACLnnspA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/triage:needs-info","name":"triage:needs-info","color":"FBCA04","default":false,"description":""},{"id":9542225587,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLOsw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:in-linear","name":"status:in-linear","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Issue or PR is now in Linear"},{"id":9542227923,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLX0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:team-assigned","name":"status:team-assigned","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"A team has been assigned the issue or PR"},{"id":10081993897,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACWO8EqQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/team:lifecycle","name":"team:lifecycle","color":"7A36AC","default":false,"description":"Issue is with the Lifecycle & Governance team"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":16,"created_at":"2026-01-22T11:32:33Z","updated_at":"2026-06-18T09:15:31Z","closed_at":"2026-06-18T09:15:31Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Bug Description\n\nI had workflow A which was calling workflow B.\nThen I moved the trigger from A to B and archived A on instance X.\nPushed the changes to instance Y.\n\nAnd now Instance Y has a published/active workflow which is archived?\n\n<img width=\"1228\" height=\"539\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d8275830-cbfc-48a9-b5c1-57c6b5a9ad08\" />\n\nBecause when I want to now \"republish\" the workflow B on instance Y:\n\n<img width=\"594\" height=\"344\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bfd452f4-b511-4a98-adea-a8755e339d02\" />\n\nSince its archived I can't.\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n1. Create workflow A and B on instance X\n2. Create any kind of webhook trigger in workflow A\n3. Call workflow B in A\n4. publish all workflows and push them to source controll on instance X\n5. pull the changes on instance Y\n6. now move the trigger from workflow A to B\n7. archive workflow A\n8. and publish workflow B\n9. publish all workflows and push them to source controll on instance X\n10. pull the changes on instance Y\n11. now republish the workflow B on instance Y\n12. see the the error as shown above\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n1. That any change pushed via source control replicates 1:1 from one instance to another, including publish like mentioned in #24563 \n2. That the workflow gets A archived and i can just publish B as I did on instance X\n\n### Debug Info\n\n# Debug info\n\n## core\n\n- n8nVersion: 2.5.0\n- platform: docker (self-hosted)\n- nodeJsVersion: 22.21.1\n- nodeEnv: production\n- database: postgres\n- executionMode: scaling (multi-main)\n- concurrency: -1\n- license: enterprise (production)\n- consumerId: d8e7ef3d-f68b-4e65-968a-f4ec4d80d59a\n\n## storage\n\n- success: all\n- error: all\n- progress: false\n- manual: true\n- binaryMode: s3\n\n## pruning\n\n- enabled: true\n- maxAge: 2160 hours\n- maxCount: 0 executions\n\n## client\n\n- userAgent: mozilla/5.0 (windows nt 10.0; win64; x64) applewebkit/537.36 (khtml, like gecko) chrome/143.0.0.0 safari/537.36\n- isTouchDevice: false\n\nGenerated at: 2026-01-22T11:31:59.496Z\n\n### Operating System\n\nWindows\n\n### n8n Version\n\n2.5.0\n\n### Node.js Version\n\n22.21.1\n\n### Database\n\nPostgreSQL\n\n### Execution mode\n\nqueue\n\n### Hosting\n\nself hosted","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/24692/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/24692/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/13966","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/13966/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/13966/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/13966/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/13966","id":2922756394,"node_id":"I_kwDOC4Q8Qs6uNbkq","number":13966,"title":"Microsoft SQL Credential not marked for first time setup after pulling from git","user":{"login":"fank","id":1900106,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MDAxMDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1900106?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank","html_url":"https://github.com/fank","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fank/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8582010757,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAAB_4cXhQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/team:nodes","name":"team:nodes","color":"7A36AC","default":false,"description":"Issue is with the Nodes team"},{"id":9542225587,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLOsw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:in-linear","name":"status:in-linear","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Issue or PR is now in Linear"},{"id":9542227923,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLX0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:team-assigned","name":"status:team-assigned","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"A team has been assigned the issue or PR"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":12,"created_at":"2025-03-16T04:10:22Z","updated_at":"2026-07-21T22:07:28Z","closed_at":"2026-07-21T22:07:26Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Bug Description\n\nI created a Microsoft SQL credential on our testing enviroment, for a workflow.\nAfter pushing and pulling it back on production I got:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a71d0ff-0dfc-40f7-99d3-70d2705d9a45)\nBut for another credential, the Microsoft SQL credential was not listed.\n\nIt is shown in the credentials but empty:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b17e27ea-e588-452f-a692-74266d7ca13e)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aba3f3ba-4346-4611-a058-d40d2d2788fc)\n\nCould it be because the stub is not empty (contains credentials)?\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"8kLeghDcRUNWeKJU\",\n  \"name\": \"Microsoft SQL account\",\n  \"type\": \"microsoftSql\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"server\": \"\",\n    \"database\": \"\",\n    \"user\": \"\",\n    \"password\": \"\",\n    \"port\": 1333,\n    \"allowUnauthorizedCerts\": true\n  },\n  \"ownedBy\": {\n    \"type\": \"personal\",\n    \"personalEmail\": \"myemail@example.tld\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n1. Create Microsoft SQL credential on environment X\n2. Push to git\n3. Pull from git on environment Y\n4. Notice its not flagged as initial setup\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nShould be flagged as initial setup required, otherwise I would not have seen it.\n\n# Debug info\n\n## core\n\n- n8nVersion: 1.81.4\n- platform: docker (self-hosted)\n- nodeJsVersion: 20.18.3\n- database: postgres\n- executionMode: scaling\n- concurrency: -1\n- license: enterprise (production)\n- consumerId: d8e7ef3d-f68b-4e65-968a-f4ec4d80d59a\n\n## storage\n\n- success: all\n- error: all\n- progress: false\n- manual: true\n- binaryMode: s3\n\n## pruning\n\n- enabled: true\n- maxAge: 336 hours\n- maxCount: 10000 executions\n\n## client\n\n- userAgent: mozilla/5.0 (windows nt 10.0; win64; x64) applewebkit/537.36 (khtml, like gecko) chrome/134.0.0.0 safari/537.36\n- isTouchDevice: false\n\nGenerated at: 2025-03-16T04:09:09.638Z\n\n### Operating System\n\ndocker (self-hosted)\n\n### n8n Version\n\n1.81.4\n\n### Node.js Version\n\n20.18.3\n\n### Database\n\nPostgreSQL\n\n### Execution mode\n\nqueue","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/13966/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/13966/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36361","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36361/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36361/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36361/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36361","id":5157143104,"node_id":"I_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAABM2PCQA","number":36361,"title":"MCP Server Trigger: tool outputSchema declares JSON Schema draft-07 - all tools silently rejected by Claude Desktop/Claude Code (2020-12-only validator)","user":{"login":"AI-Tapas","id":234867563,"node_id":"U_kgDODf_Law","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234867563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Tapas","html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Tapas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Tapas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Tapas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Tapas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Tapas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Tapas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Tapas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Tapas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Tapas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Tapas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8582010757,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAAB_4cXhQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/team:nodes","name":"team:nodes","color":"7A36AC","default":false,"description":"Issue is with the Nodes team"},{"id":9542225587,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLOsw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:in-linear","name":"status:in-linear","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Issue or PR is now in Linear"},{"id":9542227923,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLX0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:team-assigned","name":"status:team-assigned","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"A team has been assigned the issue or PR"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-08-15T02:12:07Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T08:08:17Z","closed_at":"2026-08-19T08:08:17Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bug description\n\nAs of the 13-14 Aug 2026 Claude Desktop / Claude Code update, Claude's MCP client validates tool schemas strictly against JSON Schema 2020-12 and rejects tools whose outputSchema declares draft-07. n8n's instance-level MCP server endpoint (`/mcp-server/http`) emits tool schemas with `\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"`, so every tool is rejected:\n\n```\nTool 'X' has an invalid outputSchema: JSON Schema declares an unsupported dialect (\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\")\n```\n\nThe connector shows as \"running\" in Claude's local MCP settings but zero tools appear in chat, with no visible error, so this looks like silent breakage to users.\n\n## Environment\n\nn8n version: 2.34.x (latest stable), self-hosted via Node.js on Windows.\nConnected through `npx mcp-remote http://localhost:5678/mcp-server/http`.\nClaude Desktop 1.30096.1 (Windows).\n\n## To reproduce\n\nConnect the n8n MCP endpoint to current Claude Desktop (1.30096+) and list tools.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nSchemas emitted as 2020-12 (or without an explicit draft-07 `$schema` declaration, since MCP defaults absent `$schema` to 2020-12).\n\n## Context\n\nThis is hitting the wider MCP ecosystem since the Claude update (20+ issues across server repos in 48 hours, e.g. perplexityai/modelcontextprotocol#132, anthropics/claude-code#86543). Anthropic may relax the validator, but emitting 2020-12 (or dropping the explicit draft-07 stamp) would make n8n robust either way.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36361/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36361/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}